From 19eb7c17a6a2f686097975a18812a0395dcc09b9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:08:35 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0223: Quest chain reward-item audit, two bugs fixed, four new
 items

Prep work ahead of building Replayable Quest Chains -- confirmed every
one of the 29 story quest chains resolves to a real, existing,
chainExclusive reward item before any replay mechanics get built on
top of that assumption.

Bug fixes (re-applied, never actually landed on main from an earlier
pass): 30 reward-item entries across 21 chains had a stray '@5' suffix
zeroing out the grant at three separate call sites; two chains
(the_last_clutch, the_man_who_sells_maybe) were missing the
rewardItems field entirely, which would have crashed quest resolution
outright on completion.

Four new items authored for the four chains that never had one
(the_first_haul, the_last_clutch, the_man_who_sells_maybe,
last_pilgrimage), stat-calibrated against existing same-level
chainExclusive gear rather than invented from scratch.

Also rewrites the Replayable Quest Chains backlog design doc (the
original write-up was lost at some point) to match the patch
0214/0215 itemization overhaul -- net effect is significantly less new
content required than originally planned, since padding loot is now
fully procedural and needs no new equipment defs at all.

No mechanical fields, stage data, or narrative text touched -- reward
items and four new equipment defs only.

Verified: both JSON files parse cleanly, every chain's rewardItems
resolves against equipment.json (scripted, zero gaps), npx tsc
--noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean.
