 ## Backlog
 
+### Replayable Quest Chains -- fully scoped (redesigned post-0214), ready to build
+Original design worked through end to end across several discussion
+rounds and written up here once already; that write-up has since been
+lost from this file (no record of when/why -- not resolved, not
+superseded by anything else in the log, just gone by the time this
+redesign pass started). Rewritten here in full, revised against the
+patch 0214/0215 itemization overhaul, which landed after the original
+design and invalidates a real chunk of it -- see the "what changed"
+note below before reading the rest, since several pieces that used to
+require new equipment content don't anymore.
+
+**Motivation, unchanged.** Quest chains have real loot to chase (their
+guaranteed completion `rewardItems`, `chainExclusive` unique gear) but
+are one-shot forever -- `generateChainBoard` permanently excludes any
+chain already in `completedChains`.
+
+**What changed since the original design, and why it matters here.**
+Patch 0214 replaced hand-authored padding/tiered loot with full
+procedural generation (`proceduralLoot.ts`) for everything except Sets,
+`chainExclusive` rewards, and craftables, which stay permanently
+exempt (`isProceduralTemplate()` returns false for them by construction
+-- populated `mods`/`stats` on the def). It also **deleted all 84**
+hand-duplicated `raidExclusive` `_heroic`/`_legendary` items in favor of
+one template + a `LootSourceTag`-driven budget multiplier + a bracketed
+display tag (`Iron Sword [Heroic]`). That's a direct, deliberate
+precedent this redesign follows rather than reintroduces.
+
+**Where it lives.** Unchanged: a second sub-tab on the Discovered
+Quests tab -- "Board" (existing) and "Replay Memories" (new). Extends
+the existing sub-tab system directly (`chains` joins `TAB_SUBTABS` in
+`attention.ts`).
+
+**Eligibility, unchanged.** A chain is replayable once (a) its guild
+upgrade band is owned, AND (b) the chain is already in
+`completedChains` -- both required. Owning a band never bypasses first
+clear. A chain completed before this feature existed still qualifies
+retroactively the moment its band is bought -- `completedChains` is
+read as-is, nothing to backfill.
+
+**First clear vs. replay, unchanged.** First clear stays exactly as it
+is today: always the base/"Normal" experience, no picker, a failed
+stage retries just that stage (`ActiveChain.failedStages` incrementing,
+`stage` not advancing). A **replay** is its own new structure entirely
+(not `ActiveChain` -- same reasoning as before, `ActiveRaid` is its own
+thing rather than bolted onto quest infrastructure), and a failed stage
+during a replay resets the whole attempt to stage 1, not a
+retry-in-place.
+
+**Difficulty config, unchanged in shape.** Same four scalar knobs raids
+use minus the party-specific ones: `successPenalty`, `lootBonus`,
+`durationMultiplier`. No `rewardMultiplier` -- replay changes loot only,
+gold/renown/XP stay flat. `successPenalty` applies to every stage's
+roll throughout a replay attempt, not just the final one.
+
+**Loot design, revised for the procedural system:**
+
+1. **Padding loot needs zero new equipment content.** What a stage's
+   existing dynamic loot roll already does (now procedural by default
+   for anything eligible) just needs two new `LootSourceTag` values --
+   `'chainReplayHeroic'` / `'chainReplayLegendary'` -- with their own
+   `Tuning`-editable budget multipliers, passed into the existing
+   `instantiate(defId, roll)` call exactly the way `RaidManager` already
+   passes `'raidHeroic'`/`'raidLegendary'`. `itemLevel` is each chain's
+   own `reqLevel`, not a banded approximation -- more accurate than the
+   original design's shared-band padding pools, for less work. This
+   fully replaces the original plan's ~60 new padding-pool equipment
+   defs across 6 saga bands -- **none of that content needs to exist.**
+
+2. **The dedicated item is the real chase, and needs one new (small)
+   mechanism.** `chainExclusive` rewards are permanently exempt from
+   procedural generation, same category as Sets -- `instantiate`'s
+   existing `roll` param silently no-ops for them today
+   (`if (roll && isProceduralTemplate(def))`). Explicitly decided
+   **against** reviving the just-deleted hand-duplicate-item pattern for
+   these. Instead: a new, small hybrid code path -- when a chain-exclusive
+   item is instantiated during a Heroic/Legendary replay, scale its own
+   *authored* mods/stats by a new budget multiplier (reusing the
+   `LootSourceTag`/bracket-display convention, not the "roll fresh from
+   a blank budget" path procedural items use) rather than reading fixed
+   duplicate defs. Multiplier values come from the ratios already
+   derived from real data (`knights_blade`'s and `gravewatchers_band`'s
+   own base->tier jumps, independently converging on the same range):
+   **+20-33% at Heroic, a further +25-35% on top at Legendary
+   (~+60-75% cumulative)** -- deliberately not raids' 1.5x/2.2x, which
+   were calibrated for scaling a blank template's budget, a different
+   context. No new equipment.json entries for this at all. Drops from
+   the same final stage as a chance roll (modified by the replay's
+   `lootBonus`), never guaranteed -- base tier stays exactly as-is,
+   still guaranteed, still first-clear-only.
+
+3. **Distinct display tags from raids.** Confirmed: chain-replay drops
+   get their own bracket labels, not reused `[Heroic]`/`[Legendary]`
+   text, so a player can tell at a glance whether a drop came from a
+   raid or a chain replay. Exact wording still open (something like
+   `[Replay: Heroic]`) -- pick at implementation time, not a blocking
+   design question.
+
+**Six saga bands, repurposed.** No longer needed for loot-pool grouping
+(procedural padding loot scales continuously per-chain now, no banding
+required for that). They remain exactly as designed for the **guild
+upgrade gating structure** only -- which chains a player is allowed to
+replay at all, independent of how the loot itself scales:
+
+1. **The Founding Days** (levels 1-7) -- `the_first_haul`,
+   `millers_problem`, `bandits_on_the_old_road`, `the_last_clutch`,
+   `the_man_who_sells_maybe`, `goblin_warband`, `third_crown`
+2. **The Harrower's Shadow** (levels 8-14) -- `crows_warning`,
+   `ancient_crown`, `harrowers_foot`, `something_big_in_the_foothills`,
+   `lost_kingdom`
+3. **The Wyrmfire Years** (levels 15-19) -- `demon_generals_ledger`,
+   `proving_the_bastion`, `full_moon_over_ashvale`, `dragon_hunt`,
+   `what_the_culled_become`
+4. **The Fortress Campaign** (levels 20-26) -- `granite_crossing`,
+   `demon_fortress`, `farm_at_the_edge`, `hollow_choir`
+5. **The Ashen Vigil** (levels 29-35) -- `body_snatcher_problem`,
+   `the_pale_rider`, `world_ender`, `quiet_in_millbrook`
+6. **The Last Reckoning** (levels 37-45) -- `hunt_a_lich`,
+   `the_loom_beneath`, `last_pilgrimage`, `hollow_king`
+
+**Guild upgrade gating, unchanged.** A new `ChainReplayTierDef` type
+(own array, not a reuse of `UpgradeDef.unlocks` -- needs per-entry data
+`unlocks` doesn't carry, same reason raid upgrades got their own
+`RaidUpgradeDef` instead of joining the general list): id, saga name +
+level range, description stating plainly what it does ("lets you
+replay [chains] for a chance at Heroic gear"), which chain ids belong
+to it, flat gold cost (confirmed gold-only, no growth curve -- one-time
+per band). One master unlock (reveals Replay Memories existing at all)
+plus the 6 band-specific ones, no forced ordering between bands. All 7
+cards live and are bought entirely inside Replay Memories itself, not
+Guild Hall -- same precedent as the Raid Upgrades tree living in the
+Raids panel's own Quartermaster's Den.
+
+**Replay Memories layout, unchanged.** All 6 bands always visible
+regardless of ownership (name, level range, chains covered, cost,
+Buy/Owned state). Within an owned band, only chains already in
+`completedChains` show the actual difficulty picker -- raid-styled UI,
+dedicated icon assets to be wired via the DevTool's existing
+icon-picker convention once they land in `public/`. A loot-table view
+per chain -- the dedicated item at all three tiers plus a sense of the
+level-appropriate procedural padding range -- so a player can see what
+they're chasing before committing.
+
+**Content audit and gap-fill, done as of patch 0223.** All 29 chains
+now have a real, existing, resolvable `chainExclusive` reward item --
+confirmed by script, not by inspection (every `rewardItems` entry
+resolves against `equipment.json`, zero missing fields, zero broken
+ids). Two real bugs were found and fixed along the way: a stray `@N`
+suffix (meaningful only in raid-loot parsing, meaningless here) that
+silently zeroed out 30 reward entries across 21 chains at three
+separate call sites, and two chains missing the `rewardItems` field
+entirely, which would have crashed quest resolution outright on
+completion, not just dropped the reward. Four brand-new items authored
+for the four chains that had never had one (`the_first_haul`,
+`the_last_clutch`, `the_man_who_sells_maybe`, `last_pilgrimage`),
+stat-calibrated against existing same-level items rather than invented
+from scratch.
+
+**Explicitly out of scope / decided against:** a live stat-scaling
+"calculator" for dynamic per-instance power (superseded -- the
+procedural system now does exactly this for eligible loot, and the
+hybrid multiplier approach above covers the exempt dedicated-item case
+without inventing a second one); hand-duplicated hero/legendary
+equipment defs for padding OR dedicated items (rejected twice now --
+once on the original design's own merits, and again because the
+codebase explicitly just deleted 84 of exactly this pattern); sharing
+loot pools with raids (rejected, kept separate, and now also
+tag-distinct); reusing `ActiveChain` for replay tracking (rejected, own
+structure); `rewardMultiplier` on replay difficulty (rejected,
+loot-only).
+
+**Sequencing.** Patch 0223 (this one) covers the content audit/gap-fill
+and this rewritten spec. Implementation still to come, roughly in this
+order: (1) data model -- `ChainReplayTierDef`/`ActiveChainReplay`/
+persisted ownership+progress state, no UI yet; (2) the new
+`LootSourceTag` values + budget multipliers + the dedicated-item hybrid
+scaling code path (small, no new equipment content); (3)
+`QuestManager`/`GameEngine` resolution logic -- difficulty-modified
+success, the tag-based loot resolution, reset-on-fail; (4) Replay
+Memories UI itself -- band cards, difficulty picker, loot-table view;
+(5) DevTool schema updates so the new content types are editable the
+same way everything else already is.
+
