+### Quest chain reward-item audit: two bugs fixed, four new items authored (patch 0223)
+
+```discord-update
+Dev Update | Content + Bug Fix
+
+- Fixed 21 chains that were never actually granting their promised completion reward, a stray character was breaking the lookup
+- Fixed two chains that would have crashed the game outright on completion
+- Every one of the 29 story quest chains now has its own unique item worth chasing: The First Haul, The Last Clutch, and The Man Who Sells "Maybe" get one for the first time, and The Last Pilgrimage gets a new legendary amulet
+- Rewrote the Replayable Quest Chains design doc to match the recent itemization overhaul -- less new content needed than originally planned, not more
+```
+
+Prep work ahead of building Replayable Quest Chains (see the rewritten
+Backlog entry above) -- confirmed every one of the 29 chains resolves to
+a real, existing, `chainExclusive` reward item before any replay
+mechanics get built on top of that assumption.
+
+**Bug fixes, re-applied.** The `@N` suffix issue and the two
+missing-`rewardItems`-field chains (`the_last_clutch`,
+`the_man_who_sells_maybe`) reported in an earlier pass never actually
+landed on `main`. Both fixed here for real: 30 reward-item entries
+across 21 chains had a stray `@5` suffix (meaningful only in raid
+encounter loot parsing, meaningless to chain completion's direct
+`EQUIPMENT_BY_ID[defId]` lookups) silently zeroing out the grant; two
+chains were missing the `rewardItems` field entirely despite it being
+required by `ChainDef`'s own type, which would have thrown
+`chain.rewardItems is not iterable` and crashed quest resolution
+outright on completion, not just skipped the reward.
+
+**Four new items, for the four chains that never had one.** Audited all
+29 chains directly (scripted, not by inspection) and found
+`the_first_haul`, `the_last_clutch`, `the_man_who_sells_maybe`, and
+`last_pilgrimage` had an empty or missing `rewardItems` array from the
+start -- not a bug, just never authored. New items, stat-calibrated
+against existing same-level `chainExclusive` gear (`cellar_dwellers_tooth`,
+`tollbreakers_gloves`, `loomsplinter_shard`, the Empyrean set) rather
+than invented from scratch:
+
+| Item | Chain | Level | Rarity | Slot |
+|-|-|-|-|-|
+| Quartermaster's Token | The First Haul | 1 | Uncommon | Ring |
+| Keeper's Last Feather | The Last Clutch | 5 | Uncommon | Amulet |
+| Grimsby's Loaded Coin | The Man Who Sells "Maybe" | 5 | Uncommon | Ring |
+| The Last Pilgrim's Waystone | The Last Pilgrimage | 44 | Legendary | Amulet |
+
+The Waystone is deliberately a standalone legendary, not folded into a
+set -- a new set with only one piece would be meaningless, and its
+stats were interpolated between `loomsplinter_shard` (39) and the
+Empyrean set (45) to match where the chain actually sits between them.
+All four use previously-unused accessory icon slots
+(`Accessory_03/04/16/24`).
+
+**Replayable Quest Chains design doc rewritten**, revised against the
+patch 0214/0215 itemization overhaul that landed after the original
+design -- see the Backlog entry above for the full rewrite. Net effect:
+significantly *less* new content required than the original plan, not
+more -- the ~60 padding-loot equipment defs originally scoped across 6
+saga bands are no longer needed at all now that padding loot is fully
+procedural.
+
+No mechanical fields, stage data, or narrative text touched anywhere in
+this patch -- `rewardItems` arrays and four new equipment defs only.
+
+**Verified:** both JSON files parse cleanly; every one of the 29
+chains' `rewardItems` entries resolves against `equipment.json` (zero
+missing fields, zero broken ids, zero unresolvable references,
+confirmed by script); `npx tsc --noEmit` and `npx vite build --config
+vite.web.config.ts` both pass clean.
